-- ugcportal-qn3: record, per upload, whether a minor is depicted.
--
-- Generated by `prisma migrate diff --from-migrations prisma/migrations
-- --to-schema prisma/schema.prisma --script`; the comments are the only
-- hand-edit.
--
-- NULLABLE, WITH NO DEFAULT, AND THAT IS THE POINT. Every MediaListing row
-- that already exists gets NULL, which the gate reads as "not triaged" and
-- refuses (src/lib/resale-rights.ts, blocker `triage_incomplete`). A
-- `DEFAULT 0` would have been the fail-open version of the same migration:
-- it would silently assert, about every upload anyone has ever listed, that
-- no child is shown in it — an assertion no human has made, on the one
-- question where guardian consent is the legal requirement
-- (docs/legal/manual-upload-rights-review.md § 3.5).
--
-- RightsLayer gains MINORS in the same change and needs no DDL: Prisma maps
-- enums to TEXT on SQLite, so the value is accepted by the existing
-- MediaRightsClearance.layer column the moment the schema declares it. No
-- clearance row is created here, so a depicted minor starts uncleared.

-- AlterTable
ALTER TABLE "MediaListing" ADD COLUMN "depictsMinors" BOOLEAN;
